<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20156" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hălēsus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Halaesus</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Alēsus</span></b> ), i, m., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἅλαισος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Son of Agamemnon and Clytemnestra</i> or <i>Brisēis</i>, <i>the founder
				of Falisci</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 7, 724</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10,
			352</span></i>; <i><span class="en">411</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 4,
			73</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Am. 3, 13,
			31</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>One of the Lapithœ</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 12,
				462</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A small river on the northern coast of Sicily</i>,
				<i>on which the town Halesa was situated</i>, Col.
			poët. 10, 268; <i><span class="en">Sol. 5,
		20</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
